exports[`rhachet init — two repos that ship one role slug given: [case1] alpha and beta each ship role surfer when: [t3] the sweep prices every role then: the sweep stdout matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"🧢 2 boot specs — none declare a budget
   ├─ 270 tokens (no budget)  .agent/repo=alpha/role=surfer/boot.yml (linked)
   ├─ 270 tokens (no budget)  .agent/repo=beta/role=surfer/boot.yml (linked)
   │
   └─ swept
      ├─ .agent/repo=*/role=*/boot.yml
      ├─ .behavior/*/boot.yml
      ├─ .route/*/boot.yml
      └─ src/domain.roles/*/boot.yml

   .note = a spec outside these paths is not swept. name it directly to cost it —
           \`roles cost --what <path>\`.

   .note = a \`(linked)\` spec is owned by another repo — not yours to trim. its budget is
           that repo's to raise, so \`roles boot\` warns on it rather than halts. upgrade
           the package, or raise it upstream. (2 of 2 here)

"
`;

